    {
      "obligation": "refuter:12:3",
      "id": "ex-riesz-potential-scaling-determines-the-target-exponent",
      "location": "2.2 The potential of the bump is finite and strictly positive everywhere",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The proof says that for every y in B(0,r), K_alpha(x-y) >= (|x|+r)^(alpha-n). But the in-scope definition assigns K_alpha(0)=0; when x is in B(0,r) and y=x, the left side is 0 while the right side is positive. This singleton exception does not affect the integral lower bound, which holds almost everywhere, so the gap is nonfatal.",
